---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="About | Vivid Savitri-Hampton"
  description="How I got here: HCI and industrial design, two startup exits, then agent systems and local AI operating systems deployed at Breville. Sydney, Australia."
  pathname="/about/"
>
  <article class="container-wide pt-16 pb-24" style="max-width: 1400px;">

    <div class="about-header">
      <div class="about-intro">
        <p class="small-caps mb-8">About</p>
        <h1 class="mb-8">
          I build AI systems designed to hold up in production: agentic pipelines, enterprise AI infrastructure, and governance scaffolding for teams deploying at scale.
        </h1>
      </div>
      <div class="about-portrait-wrap">
        <img
          src="/vivid-portrait.webp"
          alt="Vivid Savitri-Hampton"
          class="about-portrait"
          width="200"
          height="200"
          decoding="async"
        />
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-body">
      <p>
        I'm Vivid, based in Sydney. I build agent systems, local AI operating systems,
        and the governance scaffolding that lets other people run them.
      </p>

      <p>
        Most recently that meant Breville's first MCP-based internal tool, a custom GPT
        sitting over more than 235,000 brand assets, which I prototyped in September 2025
        and the BRG engineering team then took to production. I came to this from HCI and
        industrial design, where you cannot patch a product after it ships, so you learn
        early to ask who it fails on, and I have been asking that same question ever since
        even as the substrate keeps changing underneath it. Before any of that there were
        two startup exits in video games, one out of Shanghai and another while in Berlin, and a
        long stretch of living and working across twelve countries on four continents.
        Somewhere in the middle of all of it I did AI Product Management at Duke and an MBA
        at Steinbeis Hochschule Berlin, where my thesis was on AI-driven experience design.
      </p>

      <h2>What I work on</h2>

      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Agentic AI systems</strong>: multi-agent architectures with explicit
          safety envelopes, LLM orchestration, evaluation harnesses
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Local AI operating systems</strong>: enterprise agentic environments
          with governance scaffolding, policy controls, and safety gates built into the
          runtime. CoworkOS (Claude Cowork) and WorkspaceOS (Codex) deployed at Breville;
          KimiOS (Kimi Work) for personal use, integrating a Karpathy-style second brain
          for longitudinal reasoning
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Privacy-first AI infrastructure</strong>: provenance-aware retrieval,
          longitudinal reasoning scaffolds, human-in-the-loop review gates
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Human-AI interaction</strong>: designing experiences where AI augments
          decision-making instead of obscuring it
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Why I care about safety</h2>

      <p>
        Most AI demos look good on happy-path prompts and fall apart the moment you ask
        the hard questions: provenance, override, longitudinal change, failure modes.
      </p>

      <p>
        That's what threads my work together: <a href="/projects/vai-sante-os/">multimodal
        memory with chain-of-custody</a>, <a href="/projects/vivid-alpaca/">multi-agent
        trading with execution guardrails</a>, <a href="/projects/espresso-horoscope-mcp/">local
        agents with strict tool boundaries</a>. The use cases differ. The discipline doesn't.
      </p>

      <h2>Currently building</h2>

      <ul>
        <li>
          An AI-enabled video game, still in stealth
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://koinaku.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Koinaku</a>, a
          financial literacy app for the next generation of Indonesians, currently in
          early beta
        </li>
        <li>
          Hybrid model routing across local models (LM Studio) and OpenRouter-hosted
          models, including Qwen 3.x variants
        </li>
        <li>
          AI evaluation frameworks aimed at product decisions, not benchmark gaming
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Accolades</h2>

      <p>
        The AI work is the project list further up this page, so what follows is the decade
        before it: physical products that shipped and sold in real volume, plus a few
        hackathon results from back when AI still mostly meant a chatbot.
      </p>

      <h3>Product design</h3>

      <ul>
        <li>Red Dot Award 2022, Best of the Best: Breville Barista Express Impress BES876</li>
        <li>SCA Award 2022: Breville Barista Express Impress BES876</li>
        <li>Good Design Award 2022: Breville Joule Oven Air Pro</li>
        <li>Red Dot Award 2020: Breville Polyscience HydroPro SousVide</li>
        <li>Red Dot Award 2020: Breville Nespresso Creatista Pro</li>
        <li>IDSA 2019, Bronze: Breville Smart Oven AirFry</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Software and data</h3>

      <ul>
        <li>NASA SpaceApps 2017, 1st Place Australia / Top 25 Global</li>
        <li>NASA SpaceApps 2016, 1st Place Australia / Top 5 Global</li>
        <li>Chatfuel Chatbot 2017, Top 10 Global Finalist: Stake Chatbot</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Education</h2>

      <ul>
        <li>AI Product Management, Duke University (Pratt School of Engineering)</li>
        <li>MBA, Steinbeis Hochschule Berlin (Thesis: AI-Driven Application for Experience Design)</li>
        <li>B.A. Science, Technology, and Society, Stanford University (School of Humanities and Sciences, focus: HCI)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Languages</h2>
      <p>English · French · Mandarin</p>

      <h2>Reach out</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/vnsavitri/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a> ·
        <a href="https://github.com/vnsavitri" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a> ·
        <a href="mailto:vnsavitri@protonmail.ch">Email</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .about-header {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
    gap: 5rem;
    align-items: start;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .about-portrait {
    width: 200px;
    height: 200px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: 50% 15%;
    display: block;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .about-header {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 2rem;
    }

    .about-portrait {
      width: 140px;
      height: 140px;
    }
  }
</style>
